  "answer": "The test uses `bun:test`, so let me run the existing test first to capture the baseline failure.\nBaseline confirmed: `tokens('')` returns `['']` and whitespace isn't trimmed. Now I'll repair `src/tokens.ts`, keeping the same signature and leaving the test untouched.\nNow verify the repair by re-running the test suite:\nThe test passes. Let me also sanity-check edge cases beyond the oracle test and confirm the test file is untouched:\nRepair complete and verified.\n\n**What was wrong:** `src/tokens.ts` did a bare `value.split(',')`, so `tokens('')` returned `['']` and tokens with surrounding whitespace like `' a '` were kept verbatim.\n\n**The fix** (signature `tokens(value: string)` preserved):\n```ts\nexport function tokens(value: string) { return value.split(',').map((token) => token.trim()).filter((token) => token.length > 0) }\n```\nEach comma-separated token is trimmed, then empty tokens are filtered out.\n\n**Verification:**\n- Baseline run failed as expected (`0 pass / 1 fail`, with `tokens('')` → `[\"\"]`).\n- After the fix: `bun test` → **1 pass, 0 fail** (3 expect calls).\n- Extra edge checks: `'  x  ,\\t y\\t ,  ,,,'` → `[\"x\",\"y\"]`, `'a,,b'` → `[\"a\",\"b\"]`, `'single'` → `[\"single\"]`, `''` → `[]`.\n- `test/oracle.test.ts` (sha256 `5726a23d…`), `package.json`, and `AGENTS.md` are byte-for-byte unchanged."
